{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal involves the loss of a single family dwelling house of a size and in a location which the Council considers to be inappropriate for sub-division into more than one dwelling and there would not be a family sized unit on the ground floor and so would have an adverse effect on the character of the area generally, and on the amenities enjoyed by occupants of neighbouring property and future flats in particular, by reason of increased activity noise and general disturbance contrary to NPPF, London Plan policies D6, H1, Local Plan policies CC1, CC2, SC1, SC6, SC10.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed conversion of a single-family house into two flats by reason of their layouts on two floors, lack of evidence to ensure no disturbances between the flats, no daylight and sunlight assessment to ensure adequate light levels and outlook would not provide adequate living conditions for future occupiers contrary to National Planning Policy Framework, London Plan policies D1, D4, D6, Local Plan policies CC1, CC2, SC5.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed conversion of a single family house into two flats, by reason of position, design and external appearance of two sets of entrance gates, doors, refuse/recycle bins, cycle stores in the front garden, would be an intrusive development, out of scale and character with this and surrounding dwellings as well as  prevailing pattern of development in the locality contrary to NPPF, London Plan policies D4, D6 and Local Plan policies CC1 and CC2."
  ],
